# Phase 2: Offline Resilience, Server-Side Idempotency & Queue Management

Expand the POS offline infrastructure built in Phase 1 by adding server-side idempotency safeguards, offline queue management UI for cashiers, robust conflict handling for stock overselling/price mismatches, and background service worker sync.

---

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Server Model Change**: An `idempotency_key` column will be added to `POSTransaction` on the server database to ensure that retried offline syncs with the same `X-Idempotency-Key` never produce duplicate orders or double-deduct inventory.

> [!NOTE]
> **Queue Drawer UI**: Cashiers will be able to click the **Offline Status Badge** in the header to open a slide-over panel showing all queued transactions, sync errors, and individual retry/cancel options.

